Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [licensing gap is in the vendored Clothoids submodule, not pyclothoids]

setup.py statically compiles the BSD-2-Clause-licensed Clothoids submodule
(pyclothoids/src/Submodules/Clothoids) straight into the extension, but
upstream's own sdist/wheels carry only pyclothoids' MIT LICENSE, not
Clothoids' licence.txt. setuptools' default license_files glob
(LICEN[CS]E*) picks up a copy added at the project root with no other
packaging change, so it lands in dist-info/licenses/ beside the original.

diff --git a/LICENSE.Clothoids b/LICENSE.Clothoids
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aa9ba85
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.Clothoids
